+Gotchas that cost time:
+
+- **Formatting.** CI's `vite-plus / fmt` reads only the `fmt` block of `vite.config.ts` (print width 80, trailing commas `all`; it mirrors `nyuchi/.github/.oxfmtrc.json`). A bare `npx oxfmt` ignores it and wants to reformat ~720 files. Write a throwaway JSON file with the same values and pass it: `npx oxfmt -c /tmp/oxfmt-repo.json --check src workers`. Markdown and JSON are checked by Prettier 3.9.4 (see the pre-commit checklist); `npx vp` is not a command.
+- **Dev server.** `next dev` (Turbopack) fails on a CSS parse error: Tailwind's automatic source scan reads the literal `rounded-[var(--radius-*)]` written in prose (this file and a comment in `src/lib/mzizi-alignment.test.ts`) as a class, and Lightning CSS rejects the rule it generates (the webpack build only warns about it). Use `npx next dev --webpack` until the scan is told to skip tests and Markdown (`@source not`). It needs dummy WorkOS variables (`WORKOS_API_KEY`, `WORKOS_CLIENT_ID`, a 32+ character `WORKOS_COOKIE_PASSWORD`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKOS_REDIRECT_URI`). It also generates an untracked `AGENTS.md` at the repo root: delete it, never commit it (`no agent-local files` fails the PR).
+- **Memory.** Two `next build` processes at once on a 16 GB machine get killed; run one.
